sentences.text:
Having heard the learned advocates for the parties and perusing the material placed on record R/CR.MA/19300/2021 ORDER DATED: 21/04/2023 and taking into consideration the facts of the case, nature of allegations, gravity of offences, role attributed to the accused, without discussing the evidence in detail, at this stage, I am inclined to grant anticipatory bail to the applicant.
6. This Court has considered following aspects,
(i) learned Senior Advocate Mr.R.R.Marshal submitted that the present applicant's role is only that he dictated the Will in question, and he is neither beneficiary of the Will, nor in any way connected with the Will in question;
(ii) prima facie, dispute seems to be of civil in nature;
(ii) the present applicant does not have any past antecedents as submitted by learned advocate for the applicant;
(iv) though, relief is operating in favour of the applicant since 2021, till today, it is not reported by learned APP that the present applicant is not co-operating with the R/CR.MA/19300/2021 ORDER DATED: 21/04/2023 investigation.
7.

The applicant is ordered to be released on bail in the event of their arrest in connection with FIR C.R.No.11197005210064 of 2021 registered with Vadodara Taluka Police Station, Dist. Vadodara on executing a personal bond of Rs.10,000/-
(Rupees Ten Thousand R/CR.MA/19300/2021 ORDER DATED: 21/04/2023 Only) with one surety each of like amount on the following conditions:
(a) shall cooperate with the investigation and make himself available for interrogation whenever required;
Kiritsinh Chhatrasinh Rathod vs State Of Gujarat on 21 April, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/116548921/
2 (b) shall remain present at concerned Police Station on 27.04.2023 between 11.00 a.m. and 2.00 p.m.;
(c) shall not directly or indirectly make any inducement, threat or promise to any person acquainted with the fact of the case so as to dissuade him from disclosing such facts to the court or to any police officer;
(d) shall not obstruct or hamper the police investigation and not to play mischief with the evidence collected or yet to be collected by the police;
(e) shall at the time of execution of bond, furnish the address to the investigating officer and the court concerned and shall not change residence till the final disposal of the case till R/CR.MA/19300/2021 ORDER DATED: 21/04/2023 further orders;
(f) shall not leave India without the permission of the concerned trial court and if having passport shall deposit the same before the concerned trial court within a week; and (g) it would be open to the Investigating Officer to file an application for remand if he considers it proper and just and the learned Magistrate would decide it on merits;

